<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>The Road to Divisionals</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Oswald:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #F2F4EE;
    --surface: #E7EBE0;
    --ink: #1E2A22;
    --ink-soft: #4C5A4E;
    --line: #D6DACC;
    --rust: #BF5B1E;
    --moss: #4B6B43;
    --gold: #B4841F;
    --teal: #33627A;
    --plum: #74508F;
    --clay: #8C5A2B;
    --berry: #A0353C;
    --slate: #4A5A78;
    --grey: #7C8177;
    --shadow: none;
    --radius: 3px;
    color-scheme: light;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg: #12180F;
      --surface: #1B2317;
      --ink: #E9EEE4;
      --ink-soft: #ABB6A4;
      --line: #2C3526;
      --rust: #E07A3D;
      --moss: #83AE75;
      --gold: #D8AE4F;
      --teal: #5FA0BE;
      --plum: #A87FC4;
      --clay: #C68A50;
      --berry: #D66A70;
      --slate: #8B9DC7;
      --grey: #96998F;
      color-scheme: dark;
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg: #12180F;
    --surface: #1B2317;
    --ink: #E9EEE4;
    --ink-soft: #ABB6A4;
    --line: #2C3526;
    --rust: #E07A3D;
    --moss: #83AE75;
    --gold: #D8AE4F;
    --teal: #5FA0BE;
    --plum: #A87FC4;
    --clay: #C68A50;
    --berry: #D66A70;
    --slate: #8B9DC7;
    --grey: #96998F;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html {
    scroll-padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px);
  }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Source Sans 3", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px);
    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px);
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .page {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-family: "Oswald", "Arial Narrow", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.2px;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.9rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.05; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .num { font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "Courier New", monospace; }

  /* ---- Masthead ---- */
  .masthead { margin-bottom: 2.2rem; }
  .masthead p.sub {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    max-width: 42ch;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
  }

  /* ---- Course line (hero / nav) ---- */
  .course-wrap {
    margin: 1.8rem 0 2.6rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .course-line {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-width: 640px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0 2.1rem;
  }
  .course-track {
    position: absolute;
    top: 15px;
    left: 22px;
    right: 22px;
    height: 2px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, var(--line) 0 8px, transparent 8px 14px);
  }
  .stop {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1;
    text-align: center;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: "Source Sans 3", sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-top: 2px;
  }
  .stop .dot {
    width: 12px; height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 auto 0.5rem;
    position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }
  .stop.is-race .dot { background: var(--gold); border-color: var(--gold); width: 15px; height: 15px; }
  .stop.is-active .dot { border-color: var(--rust); background: var(--rust); }
  .stop .wk { display:block; font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .stop .race-name { display:block; font-size: 0.72rem; margin-top: 2px; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; }
  .stop.is-active .wk { color: var(--rust); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---- Guide & Strength sections ---- */
  section.block { margin-bottom: 2.6rem; }
  .guide-note, .strength-note {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .guide-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, auto) minmax(140px, auto) 1fr;
    row-gap: 0.65rem;
    column-gap: 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .guide-grid .g-label { font-weight: 600; }
  .guide-grid .g-pace { font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .guide-grid .g-feel { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .guide-grid > div { padding-bottom: 0.65rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }

  .strength-cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .strength-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .strength-cols h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .strength-cols .tag { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; display:block; }
  .strength-cols ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .strength-cols li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .strength-prog { margin-top: 1.1rem; padding-top: 0.9rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 68ch; }

  /* ---- Week tabs & calendar ---- */
  .week-tabs {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .week-tabs button {
    font-family: "Source Sans 3", sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .week-tabs button.active {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--ink);
  }
  .week-tabs button:focus-visible, .stop:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--rust); outline-offset: 2px; }

  .week-head {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.2rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .week-head .wh-title { font-family:"Oswald", sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .week-head .wh-dates { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .week-head .wh-mi { font-family:"JetBrains Mono", monospace; font-size: 1rem; }
  .week-note {
    color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0.7rem 0 1.3rem;
  }

  .day {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 76px 1fr;
    column-gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .day .d-when { padding-top: 0.15rem; }
  .day .d-day { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .day .d-date { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .day .d-mi { font-family:"JetBrains Mono", monospace; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .day .d-body { border-left: 3px solid var(--grey); padding-left: 0.9rem; }
  .day.is-race .d-body { border-left-color: var(--gold); }
  .pill-row { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    padding: 0.12rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
  }
  .d-title { font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .d-detail { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.94rem; max-width: 68ch; }

  /* ---- Rules ---- */
  .rules ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .rules li {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .rules .if { font-weight: 600; }
  .rules .then { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  footer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  <header class="masthead">
    <h1>The Road to Divisionals</h1>
    <p class="sub">Eight weeks of training from today through the Divisional Championship on November 14 — built around the races that already exist on your calendar.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="course-wrap">
    <div class="course-line" id="course-line">
      <div class="course-track"></div>
      <!-- stops injected by JS -->
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Pace &amp; effort guide</h2>
    <p class="guide-note">These are estimated starting points built from your current PRs, not measured from your actual training paces — I don't have those yet. Run by effort first, splits second. Ocean State and Twilight will give real data to sharpen every number below.</p>
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <div><span class="g-label">Easy</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">6:50–7:20 /mi</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Conversational the whole way. This is most of your mileage.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">Long run</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">6:50–7:15 /mi</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Steady and aerobic. Last mile or two can firm up if legs are fresh.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">Threshold / tempo</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">6:00–6:15 /mi</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Comfortably hard — a pace you could hold 15–20 more minutes if you had to.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">VO2 / speed reps</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">5:35–5:45 /mi (~3:28–3:35/K)</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Hard but controlled and repeatable — not the 3:20/K from Monday's session.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">5K-specific reps</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">5:44–5:50 /mi</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">The rhythm you actually want to hold at Divisionals.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">Hills</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">effort, not pace</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Powerful and hard uphill, full recovery jogging down.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">Race — controlled</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">~85–90% effort</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Dual meets. Practice rhythm, don't empty the tank.</span></div>

      <div><span class="g-label">Race — all out</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-pace">full effort</span></div>
      <div><span class="g-feel">Ocean State, Twilight, DCL, Divisional. Race the field, not a number.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Strength toolkit</h2>
    <p class="strength-note">Two short sessions a week early in the block, dropping to one as racing gets more frequent. Always paired with an easy day — never the day before a hard workout or race.</p>
    <div class="strength-cols">
      <div>
        <h3>Session A — full</h3>
        <span class="tag">~25–30 min · Weeks 1–5, then Week 7</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Single-leg RDL — 3×8 each leg</li>
          <li>Bulgarian split squat / walking lunge — 3×8 each leg</li>
          <li>Glute bridge or hip thrust — 3×12</li>
          <li>Calf raises, straight + bent knee — 3×15 each</li>
          <li>Side plank with leg lift — 2×30s each side</li>
          <li>Plank — 2×30–45s</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Session B — light</h3>
        <span class="tag">~15 min · Second weekly session, and all of Week 6 &amp; 8</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Single-leg balance reach — 2×8 each leg</li>
          <li>Clamshells or monster walks — 2×12 each side</li>
          <li>Calf raises — 2×15</li>
          <li>Plank — 2×30s</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="strength-prog">Progression: full frequency (A+B) through the peak build in Week 4–5. From Week 6 on, one session a week is enough — legs need to be fresh for racing, not sore from squats. In taper week, one short Session B on Monday only, then nothing until after Divisional.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block calendar">
    <h2>Week by week</h2>
    <div class="week-tabs" id="week-tabs"></div>
    <div id="week-panel"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="block rules">
    <h2>If this happens, do this</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="if">Legs unusually heavy before a workout</span><span class="then">Swap it for an easy run. Reattempt later in the week if there's room — don't cram it into an already-planned day.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">You miss a workout entirely</span><span class="then">Let it go. Resume the plan where you are — don't double up later to make up mileage.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">A race goes harder than planned</span><span class="then">Treat the next two days as recovery no matter what's scheduled, even if it means skipping a planned quality session.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">You feel excellent</span><span class="then">Fine to run the top of a mileage range or hit paces confidently — don't add extra volume or reps that aren't on the plan.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">Mileage is causing fatigue across several days</span><span class="then">Cut 10–15% off that week's total. A real down week beats forcing through one.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">Minor, symmetric soreness that eases as you warm up</span><span class="then">Easy running is fine. Skip strides and hard efforts until it resolves.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">Sharp, one-sided, or worsening pain</span><span class="then">Skip the run rather than modify it. Flag it to a trainer or coach if it hasn't resolved in a couple of days.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">Sick — above the neck (congestion, sore throat)</span><span class="then">Easy running is usually fine if you feel up to it. Skip the workout itself.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">Sick — below the neck (fever, chest, GI, body aches)</span><span class="then">Rest completely until it's fully gone.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">Weather wrecks a planned workout</span><span class="then">Move the session to the nearest available day or indoors rather than skip its intent. If that's not possible, just run easy — don't stack two hard days close together to compensate.</span></li>
      <li><span class="if">An unexpected meet gets added</span><span class="then">Treat it like a dual meet — controlled, not all-out — and drop whatever workout was scheduled that week to hold the line at two hard stimuli.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer>Built from your current mileage, race calendar, and history — update it as Ocean State and Twilight give real feedback on paces and recovery.</footer>
</div>

